    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738-a1">

                <pb facs="1175" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1079"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 104.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Fry to the American consul at Santiago de
                        Cuba.</hi></head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have made several ineffectual efforts to
                    communicate with you, and am at a loss to understand why the agent of a
                    Government as powerful as the United States should not at once communicate with
                    the master of an American vessel captured on <pb facs="1176" n="1080"
                        xml:id="pg1080"/> the high seas, in time of profound-peace, by a Spanish
                    man-of-war. I desire that the papers of the Virginius should be examined by you,
                    and the facts and incidents of her attempted voyage noted and communicated at
                    once, by telegraph, to the Government, as it may serve to save future
                    complications between the governments of Spain and the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOSEPH FRY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Master of the Steamship
                            Virginius, Now a prisoner in the Spanish man-of-war
                        Tornado</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
